{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544568-halloween-astral-realm-one-shot-advice","id":1544568,"title":"Halloween Astral Realm one shot advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-23T09:49:39-07:00","id":1544568,"title":"Halloween Astral Realm one shot advice","content":"I've been asked by my group to run a Halloween one shot the day after Halloween. I'm pumped for this, and decided I was gonna run it using the characters from my LA game but not really worry too much about tying it into the story of that Chronicle, just don't wanna make to make new characters basically. <br /> <br /> What should I name the Temenose realm of Halloween for this one shot and what are some ideas you can share with me about how to run it? I use to be really good and spooky stuff but it's been YEARS since I ran anything Halloween spooky and I'm drawing blanks.<br /> <br /> I've asked them for some spooky Halloween vibe fears they have, both in and out of character, zombies, ghosts, etc. but until I start getting that list I'm not really sure where to go with this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T10:06:08-07:00","id":1544571,"title":"","content":"It all depends on the kind of horror you want to run, but for a one shot, I think the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Rw4YZuRUgXA?si=sJ_jhzRAU_QKpaXX\" target=\"_blank\">Shalebridge Cradle</a> would be my recommended source of inspiration. You could make it so it was the &quot;masterpiece&quot; of a Fang of Mara that went Rapt. She remained after death as a Morphean and she is trying to make it bleed out into the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T11:11:54-07:00","id":1544579,"title":"","content":"I feel as though Halloween is not quite something with the kind of mythos or abstraction to get a distinct name beyond &quot;realm of Halloween&quot;, excepting the possibility that it might incorporate some of the influence of Nightmare Before Christmas to get a Halloweentown moniker.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't quite imagine a Temenos realm of Halloween to be a source of much genuine horror in its own right, since it's such a commercial holiday where some of the strongest emphasis is on making it accessible for young children. I think tension therein would derive from the potential to stumble unknowingly and unwillingly along paths that lead to other, related realms, some of which may menace or threaten the characters just because that's characteristic of how the behaviour of their inhabitants*, and some of which function as large scale nightmare realms in which one is in danger of constant direct psychic attack be the fears and horrors of people at large.<br /> <br /> I can see a scenario in which the Halloween realm has a draw for the insights it can provide into how Sleepers relate to the notion of supernatural monsters when viewed through a safe, curated lens, but there's so much tied up in the holiday that it provides a notably high amount of possible diversions and tangents, some of which can be dangerous.<br /> <br /> And maybe a notion that the realm has a property that goes beyond the norm of the Temenos and into a distinct Mystery; that on the holiday itself, its realm seems to be unusually well-connected into the primal realms of pure fear and Horror that lie along the boundary separating Temenos from Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Oh, also the Realm of the Dead. Halloween might carry just enough connotations of the original Gaelic holiday (as well as the symbolic paths away from its use of ghost and grave symbols) to connect to the Astral Realm representing the undifferentiated concept of death, which can carry its own kinds of hazards (not least of which is the possibility that actual ghosts from the Underworld might drift in there and start causing problems).<br /> <br /> * For instance, while I imagine a lot of movie monsters and the like won't be genuinely scary to the Awakened, they're still going to act out the part of things that will assault them, which can at least be a source of pressure and injury to their dream bodies that they would prefer to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T09:40:02-07:00","id":1544657,"title":"","content":"I think I like the idea of the realm being layered.<br /> <br /> The first layer, the one people first encounter when arriving, is a maze of streets and houses and becomes more claustrophobic and complicated the deeper you go. It's mostly harmless and is the fun, silly, trick or treat aspect of the realm. The deeper the maze goes the closer you get to the second layer, which is filled with all things horror, but movie style. Things like zombies, ghosts, and other Halloween movies hangs out there, probably drastically changing in power year to year to reflect whatever is making it into movie theaters that year. The third layer is mind numbing fear, just the essence of fear. DO NOT TOUCH signs posted everywhere by other awakened, and from there the Animia Mundi monsters sometimes slip through <br /> <br /> Probably gonna call it something silly like &quot;Terror Town&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> And then the one shot will be dealing with some Anima Mundi, primal fear monster that has slipped through the cracks and into the second layer.<br /> <br /> So the one shot will be about moving through the first layer into the second layer, containing the terror Goetia, and then making their way to the door to the third layer and toss it back in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}